{
  "_doc": "Trees, shrubs and rocks of the landscape (owner 2026-10-07: 'Baguio City must be filled with different kinds of trees, not just pine trees'). Archetypes are modelled by model/blender/flora.py at ref_height_m; species pick an archetype, a tint (foliage, or blossom for flowering trees) and a height range. Heights, colours and the zone shares are ESTIMATEs; the species and the pine's share are cited. Zones: forest = WorldCover tree cover away from buildings and OSM woods; urban = tree cover among buildings, OSM single trees and tree rows; park = OSM parks and gardens.",
  "sources": {
    "S1": "SunStar Baguio, 'Baguio City wants tree cutting stopped' (2020-07-13), https://www.sunstar.com.ph/baguio/local-news/baguio-city-wants-tree-cutting-stopped : 492,974 Benguet pines, 19.7% of the city's trees; the other 80.3% ornamental and exotic: Alnus, Eucalyptus, Calliandra, African Tulip, Agoho, Cypress, Bottle Brush, Coral Tree, Paper Bark Tree, Norfolk Pine, Maple and Balete.",
    "S2": "Wikipedia, 'Burnham Park (Baguio)', read 2026-10-07, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burnham_Park_(Baguio) : about 2,600 trees (2015); 72 species in a 2009 inventory (19 trees); most common families Myrtaceae, Moraceae and Bignoniaceae; Benguet pine, pink shower and African tuliptree among the prevalent trees.",
    "S3": "Wikipedia, 'Pinus kesiya', read 2026-10-07, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinus_kesiya : up to 30-35 m tall with a straight, cylindrical trunk; Baguio, 'The City of Pines', is noted for large stands of it.",
    "S4": "University of Baguio research abstract, 'Inventory and Assessment of the Floristic Composition of Burnham Park' (via web search 2026-10-07): Cupressus sempervirens and Araucaria bidwillii listed among the park's trees."
  },
